DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI PowerFlowDashboardPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
over an injectable PowerFlowDataSource seam (default = a sunny-midday SI sample + a 48-point diurnal
history); an adaptive layout (macOS/iPad regular vs iPhone compact) using the P2 tokens + P3 shared
components — TSGlassPanel/TSCard/TSChartContainer/TSAreaChart/TSLineChart/TSEmptyState/TSErrorDisplay/
TSButton/TSSelect/TSMetricBar/TSIconBox/typography — with the live status badges, four current-power
stat cards (with direction sublabels), the battery-state panel (SOC bar + energy remaining + total
capacity), the directional power-flow diagram, the range-scoped stacked power-over-time area chart,
and the battery state-of-charge line chart. Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings
with web key names; full VoiceOver labels/traits; power/energy convert to W/kW · Wh/kWh at the render
boundary from SI. Deep-linkable via the new .powerFlow route (AppRouteParser resolves /power-flow
automatically) and hosted through the shell's route registry. Verified on BOTH idioms: macOS app
build SUCCEEDED, macOS unit tests 18/18, iOS (arm64 simulator) app build SUCCEEDED — with the two
pre-existing out-of-scope blockers neutralised local-only and reverted. ZERO diagnostics in any of
my files across every build.

